     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual inpatient ceiling is 2,400 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
