       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. You've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is well beyond any labeled or guideline-supported dose. No indication I know of calls for it. The risk of serious harm, mainly GI hemorrhage and acute kidney injury, is high, and it would be hard to reverse once the doses were given.\n\nYou can still get this done:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** I can enter 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day) right away.\n- **Call inpatient pharmacy or the attending:** If you think this patient needs an exception, they can review it and approve it. They may also suggest a different regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen or another analgesic.\n- **Tell me what you're treating:** If you give me the indication, such as pain, inflammation, or fever, I can help you find an effective regimen.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
